  <text>
    <body>
      <conceptEntry id="dpp-0128">
      <languageSection xml:lang="eng">
          <descrip type="definition">
            <p>lens-scoped attestation consisting of an attester signature over the subject, the subject state commitment, the lens identity and version, the mode (live or snapshot), a verdict with coverage report, and log-anchored time</p>
          </descrip>
          <note type="note">Stamps accrete append-only and are valid under the stamper's lens regardless of the issuer's.</note>
          <note type="note">Jurisdiction stamps on a foreign-issued passport correspond to visas; entry and exit stamps correspond to verifier custody events.</note>
          <note type="note">Stamps may carry quantity context, inherited by downstream transformations.</note>
          <ref>UniDPP PLAN (2026-09) Semantic exchange, stamps, and the transformation algebra</ref>
      </languageSection>
      </conceptEntry>
    </body>
  </text>
</tbx>
